component SigilSkillCompatibility {
  goal {
    Validate one portable skill compatibility declaration identically across hosts
    before any workspace semantic interpretation.

    Keep compatibility schema, stable caret-range policy, and failure reporting
    separate from the skill module index and workspace bootstrap orchestration.
  }

  interface {
    SkillCompatibility {
      compatibility.json is an exact JSON object with required string properties
      cliVersion, coreVersion, and sigilVersion and no unknown properties

      cliVersion and coreVersion contain stable caret expressions over complete
      semantic versions; sigilVersion contains one exact stable semantic version

      validate(metadataPath, actualCliVersion, actualCoreVersion,
      configuredSigilVersion) returns compatible or returns incompatible evidence
      containing the metadata path, failure reason, declared expectations, and
      available actual versions

      missing, unreadable, malformed, unknown-property, prerelease, or incompatible
      input returns incompatible before workspace interpretation and performs no
      mutation
    }
  }
}

expand SigilSkillCompatibility {
  logic {
    SkillCompatibility {
      Require exactly cliVersion, coreVersion, and sigilVersion as string properties.

      Parse CLI and core declarations only as ^M.m.p with nonnegative integer major,
      minor, and patch identifiers and no prerelease. Ignore build metadata for
      precedence but reject incomplete versions and every prerelease declaration or
      actual version.

      For ^M.m.p where M is greater than zero, accept stable actual versions at least
      M.m.p and less than (M+1).0.0. For ^0.m.p where m is greater than zero, accept
      stable actual versions at least 0.m.p and less than 0.(m+1).0. For ^0.0.p,
      accept only stable versions at least 0.0.p and less than 0.0.(p+1).

      Require configuredSigilVersion to equal the declared stable sigilVersion after
      ignoring build metadata for precedence.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    SkillCompatibility {
      compatibility.json is required and must be readable and valid before the skill
      relies on CLI, core, or workspace semantics.

      Hosts use this exact schema and range policy rather than a host-library
      default.

      Compatibility failure reports evidence and never initializes, rewrites, or
      interprets the selected workspace.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    SkillCompatibilityBoundary {
      Decision: Own an exact three-property schema, stable caret-range evaluation for
      CLI and core, and exact stable Sigil language-version equality in one focused
      component.

      Scope: Governs portable skill bootstrap compatibility; excludes installation
      discovery and mutation of incompatible artifacts.

      Trade-offs: Prerelease toolchains are rejected and the workflow owns a small
      fixed range grammar instead of deferring it to host libraries.

      Design issues addressed: Host-specific parsers, ambiguous prerelease matching,
      and malformed metadata can make portable workflow behavior diverge.

      Discarded alternatives: Host-library default range semantics, permissive
      unknown properties, and implicit prerelease matching were rejected.

      Consequences: Every host reaches the same compatibility result and stops with
      comparable evidence before unsupported workspace interpretation.
    }
  }

  cases {
    SkillCompatibility {
      With declared range ^0.8.0, stable 0.8.0 and 0.7.4 are compatible, while 0.8.0,
      0.7.1-beta.1, and a prerelease declaration are incompatible.

      Missing, unreadable, non-object, missing-property, non-string, or unknown-
      property metadata reports its exact reason and performs no workspace
      interpretation or mutation.

      An incompatible stable version reports the declared expectation and available
      actual version and stops before workspace interpretation.
    }
  }
}
